# A pinwheel program: a central great room that must touch all four habitable
# rooms around it at once. With four daylight-needing arms forced to the
# perimeter, no band row and no slicing tree can also seat the great room against
# all four — only the rectangular-dual topology can. `barndsl layout
# examples/pinwheel.brief` (the default `fill` engine) detects that bands/slice
# leave an adjacency unmet and picks the dual. (The program has no bathroom, so
# the compiler notes a NO_BATH warning — add one and the four arms still pin it.)
plan "Pinwheel"
ceiling 10

room great:   living   area 320
room north:   bedroom  area 182
room east:    bedroom  area 168
room south:   kitchen  area 210
room west:    bedroom  area 154

adjacent great north east south west
